<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis weak around Kansas mills.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis weak around Kansas mills.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were cut at many locations in Kansas serving mills although elsewhere levels were mostly steady, merchandisers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The flour mills here (in Kansas) are pretty much covered for right now,&quot; one Kansas merchandiser said.</p>
<p>Bids were cut up to seven cents in Colby, Wichita, Newton and Topeka and were seen remaining weak at least until the end of the month.</p>
<p>Warm, sunny weather was reported in Oklahoma and Kansas with temperatures seen rising to the upper 70s Fahrenheit.  </p>
